# hopsworks client log (cli interface)
# crashed=True  markers=['Connection closed']

===== client errors (agent transcript) =====
Usage: hops alert job create [OPTIONS] JOB_NAME

  Create an alert that fires on a job event (e.g. ``failed``).

  Args:     ctx: Click context.     job_name: The job name.     receiver:
  Receiver name the alert notifies.     status: Job event that triggers the
  alert.     severity: Alert severity.

Options:
  --receiver TEXT                 Alert receiver name.  [required]
  --status [finished|failed|killed|long_running]
                                  [required]
  --severity [warning|critical|info]
                                  [required]
  --json                          Output as JSON (machine-readable; for LLMs
                                  and scripts).
  --verify / --no-verify          Verify the Hopsworks TLS certificate; --no-
                                  verify skips verification for self-signed /
                                  IP-SAN-mismatched certs.
  -h, --help                      Show this message and exit.
===RECEIVER CREATE===
Usage: hops alert receiver create [OPTIONS] NAME

  Create an alert receiver. Provide exactly one channel type.

  Args:     ctx: Click context.     name: Receiver name.     email: Email
  recipients.     slack: Slack channels.     pagerduty:
  ``service_key:routing_key`` pairs.     webhook: Webhook URLs.
  send_resolved: Notify on resolution too.

Options:
  --email TEXT            Email recipient; repeatable.
  --slack TEXT            Slack channel; repeatable.
  --pagerduty TEXT        PagerDuty "service_key:routing_key"; repeatable.
  --webhook TEXT          Webhook URL; repeatable.
  --send-resolved         Also notify when the alert resolves.
  --json                  Output as JSON (machine-readable; for LLMs and
                          scripts).
  --verify / --no-verify  Verify the Hopsworks TLS certificate; --no-verify
                          skips verification for self-signed / IP-SAN-
                          mismatched certs.
  -h, --help              Show this message and exit.
